+# Sourced inspiration note
+
+## Parallel cited
+
+A motif-level parallel is the journey through a threshold in “Inana's descent to the nether world,” composition 1.4.1 in the University of Oxford's Electronic Text Corpus of Sumerian Literature (ETCSL), composite text: <https://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/section1/tr141.htm>. The page's opening lines describe Inana's descent; lines 122–163 describe entry through seven gates and the removal of items of dress and regalia. This fixture uses a shore threshold and a shared bowl as original imagery; it does not retell that composition or import its characters, plot, sequence, or named objects.
+
+## Attribution question
+
+The reference for this comparison is attributed to the ETCSL page and its named composition above. This note does not assert an individual ancient author or reproduce the modern translation. Attribution to the cited page is separate from any rights conclusion.
+
+## Rights question
+
+The rights status of the ETCSL site's modern presentation, editorial work, and translation has not been determined here. Consult the corpus's credits/copyright information and applicable terms before reproducing any protected expression. The age of an underlying ancient composition does not by itself answer the rights question for a modern translation or edition.
+
+## AI-training-permission question
+
+AI-training permission has not been assessed or established. Public accessibility, attribution, and any conclusion about copyright status do not imply permission for AI training; that permission question remains separate and unanswered.
+
+This note records sourced inspiration only. It is not an in-world source and supplies no fictional canon.
