+# Symbolism clause map — Low-Water Hymn
+
+Source text: the newly authored fictional `lowwater-hymn-excerpt.md`, attributed to in-world source ID `lowwater-hymn`.
+
+| Clause | Editorial symbolism reading | Limit |
+|---|---|---|
+| “At low water” | A moment of exposure or transition in this poem. | Does not establish a calendar, tide table, or cosmology. |
+| “the shell ring” | A possible image of a boundary made collectively. | Not a legal seal, faction emblem, or proof of alliance. |
+| “beside the bowl” | The bowl may mark a place for shared attention. | No entity ID or physical artifact is asserted by the poem. |
+| “The bowl keeps no name” | A reading of withheld or unclaimed identity. | Does not establish that names are erased in-world. |
+| “no voice owns the tide” | A possible refusal of exclusive control over a recurring force. | Metaphorical reading only; it does not define faction law. |
+| “pass the reed-bell hand to hand” | A possible image of shared responsibility. | Does not prove that the Shellweavers or Reedwardens jointly handled the fixture's Reed Bell. |
+| “let the water return it” | A possible image of release or renewal. | Does not assert supernatural return, causation, or an objective event. |
+
+These are interpretive readings of authored words, not new canon. The checker does not read this map or the excerpt.
